<!--
  A sample Apple Health export, for SLOP1638.

  Nothing on the site reads this at the moment. It was made for a sleep reader
  on the week 1 lab, which the author has since taken off the page; the reader
  and this file were both kept rather than deleted. It is still what
  spec/health-export.test.ts runs against, so it is not dead weight.

  Every record in it was generated. It describes nobody: there is no person
  called Ada, no watch, and no night. That was the point from the start, because
  a course that demonstrated with a real export would be publishing somebody's
  sleep history permanently, and a later deletion would not retract it.

  What it carries, because each of these is a shape the reader has to survive:

    * one night recorded by two sources at once, a watch and a phone, which is
      what an ordinary export holds and what must never be silently merged
    * the staged shape, Core, Deep, REM and Awake, which exists only in exports
      written by watchOS 9 and iOS 16 and later
    * the unstaged shape, in bed and asleep, which is all an older instrument
      could say and is a complete record rather than a broken one
    * a short afternoon stretch, inside the midday to midday window the reader
      uses and outside the night itself
    * a second night, which the reader is expected to discard
    * heart rate, steps, a workout and an activity summary, which is what the
      hundreds of megabytes of a real export are actually made of
    * records with MetadataEntry children, so the tag scanner cannot assume a
      Record is self closing, and escaped characters in attribute values

  The DOCTYPE below is Apple's, trimmed to the elements this file uses.
-->
<!DOCTYPE HealthData [
<!ELEMENT HealthData (ExportDate,Me,(Record|Correlation|Workout|ActivitySummary)*)>
<!ATTLIST HealthData locale CDATA #REQUIRED>
<!ELEMENT ExportDate EMPTY>
<!ATTLIST ExportDate value CDATA #REQUIRED>
<!ELEMENT Me EMPTY>
<!ELEMENT Record (MetadataEntry*)>
<!ELEMENT MetadataEntry EMPTY>
<!ELEMENT Correlation (MetadataEntry*,Record*)>
<!ELEMENT Workout (MetadataEntry*)>
<!ELEMENT ActivitySummary EMPTY>
]>
